     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is 5 times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock. This patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order is authorized.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If it was 5 mg or 10 mg, I can enter it once a clinician confirms.\n- If the prescriber really does intend 50 mg, they should enter and document it themselves, and pharmacy should review it."
      }
     ],
