       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either concern.\n\n- **Safety:** 50 mg is 5 times the maximum adult dose of 10 mg daily. Because you're not the prescriber, your confirmation doesn't show that a clinician intended this dose. The order could cause serious harm if it were given.\n- **Authorization:** Orders need to come from a licensed prescriber.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the patient's prescriber to review the order. If they meant a standard dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, they can tell me or enter it themselves.\n- If they do intend a dose above the maximum, they should enter it directly. Pharmacy will need to review it and verify it.\n\nI'm glad to enter the order as soon as a clinician gives a dose within the recommended range."
